  <article class="max-w-2xl mx-auto prose-reader">
    <h1 class="font-serif text-3xl font-medium text-[var(--color-ink)] leading-tight mb-6">
      About
    </h1>

    <p>
      I’m Nora — a trans woman from Seattle, living in Barcelona. I write short
      fiction, essays and the occasional poem. Some of it is true. Some of it is
      about a competitive eater named Jim.
    </p>

    <p>
      My days are spent in the sun, in community with friends and chosen family.
      I explore beautiful architecture with my eyes and a camera, eat my way
      through a maze of Latin, Asian and Mediterranean food, and find ways to
      make street signs look queer. I talk to strangers. I write my phone number
      in books and then donate them. I like the kind of risk where the odds
      aren’t purely mathematical — where if it works out, the only available
      explanation is fate.
    </p>

    <p>
      This is where I put the writing I want in the world. If something here
      lands, tell me. I’m a parasite when it comes to compliments from strangers.
    </p>

    <p>
      Reach me at
      <a href="mailto:hello@novellanora.com">hello@novellanora.com</a>.
    </p>
  </article>
</Base>
